{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/832440-fetishes-that-either-hate-the-user-are-banes-or-otherwise-unpleasantly-in-service","id":832440,"title":"Fetishes that either hate the user, are banes, or otherwise unpleasantly in service","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-18T04:29:45-08:00","id":832440,"title":"Fetishes that either hate the user, are banes, or otherwise unpleasantly in service","content":"So I was just wondering what to do with such fetishes. So far, in one game i've had my players get rewarded for mediating a wendigo-Talon vs European caern dispute (read-Taking a side to ensure no phyric victory is to be had. Was very surprised that they went against the europeans. The majority of them are white homids.) and they got mad loot for that. In another game, the player has participated in two multi-pack battles with spirals in which the mentor/pack leader secured items for her. In simple we've just had rites of cleansing drive the bane out and a new rite used over the attractive item to make a gaian fetish. But while creating a new spirit (and new taboos) is interesting roleplay, it'd be interesting to go with an item that hates it's user too. <br /> <br /> Problem is; This is too simple I think. <br /> - Uktena use banes and other things best not used just fine. <br /> -Get of Fenrir theurges allegedly control spirits by threatening them into service. (another argument is that they do everything just like everyone else, with high quality items to bribe)<br /> -Glass walkers use weaver spirits and multi-spirit techniques<br /> - Fianna and black furies tie loads of pointless bans and taboos to their fetishes. How do i make them known?<br /> - Items like the devil-whip are made with unusual construction (it's a bane's severed tentacle, with a spirit inside it keeping it solid) I haven't put one into either game yet, but a player wants a whip, and I'd be happy to oblige. <br /> <br /> So, Like, If a player just picks, attunes and uses a Bane fetish, what's supposed to happen? Can players just talk with their fetishes to know their bans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T11:13:07-08:00","id":832614,"title":"","content":"Uh... any Garou could use a bane-empowered fetish, but the werewolf is gonna be tainted by using it. Purifying the cursed weapon or tool isn't something a simple rite of cleansing will fix, generally speaking. Unless the player wants to be marked as an enemy of the Nation, and be barred from coming anywhere near a Caern on pain of violating the Litany, they will likely destroy such items.<br /> <br /> Using fetishes is instinctive- picking up or touching a fetish will trigger a Gnosis roll, and if successful, the Garou and the slumbering spirit powering the item will instinctively commune and the Garou can understand and use the item. Spirits kept within fetishes are generally not active and conversing with them through speech is generally not possible unless they are released (either through the destruction of the item or by terms being violated).<br /> <br /> The Uktena do not situation is a bit more nuanced than that also. Bane tenders keeping banes trapped within spiritual prisons, or using parts of dead banes in conjunction with Gaian spirits (like the baneskin) are more up their alley. They are rumored to keep powerful and evil fetishes hidden away, but the Uktena are certainly not just using the dread things willy-nilly.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about the Fianna or Black Furies, so I can't comment on bans associated with their fetishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:51:51-08:00","id":832935,"title":"","content":"Fetishes should work fine as normal in terms of game mechanics.<br /> <br /> However, I would add lots of flavor text to portray the use of Bane fetishes as negative. If the fetish does damage, I would describe the wounds it inflicts as very gruesome. Other kinds of effects may leave some kind of unpleasant after effect. I might tell the player he begins to have nightmares, or he begins looking ragged or emitting foul odors. Or he has minor bad luck - stubbing his toe, getting tears in his clothing.<br /> <br /> In legend, cursed items eventually turn on their owners and lead them to destruction. However, unless it is meant as a plot point, I'd avoid anything too drastic.<br /> <br /> I assume as part of the attunement process, the Garou learns what the bans are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}